" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186186629 #edb/ref 1080 "\\frac{34}{9}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186186629 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186186629 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "08a51dff-0f49-52c1-ab38-9208cc65b517" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186188043 #edb/ref 1069 "e-10340" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186188043 #edb/ref 1071 "${3x^{2},\\begin{vmatrix}0 \\le x \\le 1 \\\\ 0,\\end{vmatrix}otherwise$\n\nLet $X$ and $Y$ be continuous random variables.\nFind the conditional variance $\\textrm{Var}\\big\\begin{bmatrix}X \\, & \\, Y=-2\\big\\end{bmatrix}$ given that the conditional probability density function $f_{X\\mid Y}(x \\, \\mid \\, -2)$ is shown above and the corresponding expected value is $\\mu_{X \\mid -2}=\\dfrac{3}{4}$." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186188043 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "ea6a79c4-09fc-5ae9-9e92-e7bacd4939d9" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186188043 #edb/ref 1074 "Recall that the conditional variance of $X$ given $Y=y$ is defined by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nVar\\begin{bmatrix}X & Y = y\\end{bmatrix} &= E\\begin{bmatrix}(X - μ_{X \\mid y})^{2} & Y = y\\end{bmatrix} \\\\\n&= E\\begin{bmatrix}X^{2} & Y = y\\end{bmatrix} - μ_{X \\mid y}^{2}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere\n\n$$\n\\textrm{E}\\big\\begin{bmatrix}X^2 \\, & \\, Y=y \\big\\end{bmatrix} = \\int_{-\\infty}^{\\infty} x^2 \\, f_{X\\mid Y}(x \\, \\mid \\, y) \\: \\textrm{d}x\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nE\\begin{bmatrix}X^{2} & Y =-2\\end{bmatrix} &= \\int_{- ∞}^{∞}x^{2}f_{X\\mid Y}(x \\mid - 2)dx \\\\\n&= \\int_{0}^{1}x^{2} \\cdot 3x^{2}dx \\\\\n&= \\int_{0}^{1}3x^{4}dx \\\\\n&= [\\frac{3x^{5}}{5}]_{0}^{1} \\\\\n&= \\frac{3}{5} - 0 \\\\\n&= \\frac{3}{5}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nVar\\begin{bmatrix}X & Y =-2\\end{bmatrix} &= E\\begin{bmatrix}X^{2} & Y =-2\\end{bmatrix} - μ_{X \\mid - 2}^{2} \\\\\n&= \\frac{3}{5} - (\\frac{3}{4})^{2} \\\\\n&= \\frac{3}{5} - \\frac{9}{16} \\\\\n&= \\frac{3}{80}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186188044 #edb/ref 1069 "e-10341" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186188044 #edb/ref 1071 "${\\frac{3}{y^{4}},\\begin{vmatrix}y \\ge 1 \\\\ 0,\\end{vmatrix}otherwise$\n\nLet $X$ and $Y$ be continuous random variables.\nFind the conditional variance $\\textrm{Var}\\big\\begin{bmatrix}Y \\, & \\, X=3\\big\\end{bmatrix}$ given that the conditional probability density function $f_{Y\\mid X}(y \\, \\mid \\, 3)$ is shown above and the corresponding expected value is $\\mu_{Y \\mid 3}=\\dfrac{3}{2}$." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186188044 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "fef21fcb-bab6-5f33-a792-280e28a97f81" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186188044 #edb/ref 1074 "Recall that the conditional variance of $Y$ given $X=x$ is defined by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nVar\\begin{bmatrix}Y & X = x\\end{bmatrix} &= E\\begin{bmatrix}(Y - μ_{Y \\mid x})^{2} & X = x\\end{bmatrix} \\\\\n&= E\\begin{bmatrix}Y^{2} & X = x\\end{bmatrix} - μ_{Y \\mid x}^{2}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere\n\n$$\n\\textrm{E}\\big\\begin{bmatrix}Y^2 \\, & \\, X=x \\big\\end{bmatrix} = \\int_{-\\infty}^{\\infty} y^2 \\, f_{Y\\mid X}(y \\, \\mid \\, x) \\: \\textrm{d}y\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nE\\begin{bmatrix}Y^{2} & X = 3\\end{bmatrix} &= \\int_{- ∞}^{∞}y^{2}f_{Y\\mid X}(y \\mid 3)dy \\\\\n&= \\int_{1}^{∞}y^{2} \\cdot \\frac{3}{y^{4}}dy \\\\\n&= \\int_{1}^{∞}\\frac{3}{y^{2}}dy \\\\\n&= \\int_{1}^{∞}3y^{-2}dy \\\\\n&= [3 \\cdot (y^{-1})/((-1))]_{1}^{∞} \\\\\n&= [- \\frac{3}{y}]_{1}^{∞} \\\\\n&= 0 - (-3) \\\\\n&= 3\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nVar\\begin{bmatrix}Y & X = 3\\end{bmatrix} &= E\\begin{bmatrix}Y^{2} & X = 3\\end{bmatrix} - μ_{Y \\mid 3}^{2} \\\\\n&= 3 - (\\frac{3}{2})^{2} \\\\\n&= 3 - \\frac{9}{4} \\\\\n&= \\frac{3}{4}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186188045 #edb/ref 1069 "e-10342" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186188045 #edb/ref 1071 "$f(x, y) = {2y\\ln (x),\\begin{vmatrix}1 \\le x \\le e, 0 \\le y \\le 1, \\\\ 0,\\end{vmatrix}otherwisef_{X}(x) = {\\ln (x),\\begin{vmatrix}1 \\le x \\le e, \\\\ 0,\\end{vmatrix}otherwise$\n\nLet $X$ and $Y$ be continuous random variables. Their joint probability density function and the marginal probability density function of $X$ are shown above. Find the conditional variance $\\textrm{Var}\\big\\begin{bmatrix}Y \\,\\big & \\, X=1 \\big\\end{bmatrix}$ given that the corresponding expected value is $\\mu_{Y \\mid 1}=\\dfrac{2}{3}$." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186188045 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "acb4923c-ce04-5cd5-af01-2f078a18ceed" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186188045 #edb/ref 1074 "Recall that the conditional variance of $Y$ given $X=x$ is defined by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nVar\\begin{bmatrix}Y & X = x\\end{bmatrix} &= E\\begin{bmatrix}(Y - μ_{Y \\mid x})^{2} & X = x\\end{bmatrix} \\\\\n&= E\\begin{bmatrix}Y^{2} & X = x\\end{bmatrix} - μ_{Y \\mid x}^{2}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere\n\n$$\n\\textrm{E}\\big\\begin{bmatrix}Y^2 \\, & \\, X=x \\big\\end{bmatrix} = \\int_{-\\infty}^{\\infty} y^2 \\, f_{Y\\mid X}(y \\, \\mid \\, x) \\: \\textrm{d}y\n$$\n\nNote that\n\n$$\n\\textrm E\\big\\begin{bmatrix}Y \\, & \\, X = x \\big\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nis a function of $x$.\n\nThe conditional density function of $Y$ given $X=x$ can be computed as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nf_{Y\\mid X}(y \\mid x) &= (f(x, y))/(f_{X}(x)) \\\\\n&= (2y\\ln (x))/(\\ln (x)) \\\\\n&= 2y\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere\n\n$$\n1 \\leq x \\leq e, \\: 0 \\leq y \\leq 1\n$$\n\nOutside this domain, we have\n\n$$\nf_{Y \\mid X} (y \\, \\mid \\, x) = 0\n$$\n\nNotice that $f_{Y \\mid X} (y \\, \\mid \\, x)$ does not depend on $x$. Therefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nE\\begin{bmatrix}Y^{2} & X = 1\\end{bmatrix} &= \\int_{- ∞}^{∞}y^{2}f_{Y\\mid X}(y \\mid 1)dy \\\\\n&= \\int_{0}^{1}y^{2} \\cdot 2ydy \\\\\n&= \\int_{0}^{1}2y^{3}dy \\\\\n&= [\\frac{y^{4}}{2}]_{0}^{1} \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{2}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nVar\\begin{bmatrix}Y & X = 1\\end{bmatrix} &= E\\begin{bmatrix}Y^{2} & X = 1\\end{bmatrix} - μ_{Y \\mid 1}^{2} \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{2} - (\\frac{2}{3})^{2} \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{2} - \\frac{4}{9} \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{18}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186188336 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186049871 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186188336 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186050965 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186188336 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186188655 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186188336 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186188721 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186188336 #edb/ref 1039 "Calculating a Conditional Variance Given a Conditional PDF" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186188336 #edb/ref 1041 #edb/ref 17592186188043 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186188336 #edb/ref 1042 #uuid "29e185b1-7bd3-5441-b502-3049a253cf3e" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186188337 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186188722 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186188337 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186188724 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186188337 #edb/ref 1039 "Calculating a Conditional Variance Given a Conditional PDF Using Improper Integrals" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186188337 #edb/ref 1041 #edb/ref 17592186188044 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186188337 #edb/ref 1042 #uuid "aadf2ac8-bfb4-5371-97c3-1ae194c9479f" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186188338 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186188661 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186188338 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186188719 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186188338 #edb/ref 1039 "Calculating a Conditional Variance Given Joint and Marginal Density Functions" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186188338 #edb/ref 1041 #edb/ref 17592186188045 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186188338 #edb/ref 1042 #uuid "fa6c30c5-e8c2-502d-abac-5d54f0b6f2fc" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186188512 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186189179 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186188512 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186189180 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186188512 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186189181 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186188512 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186189182 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186188512 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186189203 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186188512 #edb/ref 1044 #edb/ref 17592186045463 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186188512 #edb/ref 1045 "Conditional Variance for Continuous Random Variables" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186188512 #edb/ref 1046 #edb/ref 17592186189179 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186188512 #edb/ref 1049 #edb/ref 17592186049908 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186188512 #edb/ref 1053 #uuid "831069d2-736b-52d1-a2bb-6631187686b5" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186188724 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186186624 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186188724 #edb/ref 1069 "q-146806" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186188724 #edb/ref 1071 "$f_{X\\mid Y}(x \\mid - 2) = {\\frac{4}{x^{5}},\\begin{vmatrix}x \\ge 1 \\\\ 0,\\end{vmatrix}otherwise$\n\nLet $X$ and $Y$ be continuous random variables.\nFind the conditional variance $Var\\begin{bmatrix}X & Y =-2\\end{bmatrix}$ given that the conditional probability density function $f_{X\\mid Y}(x \\mid - 2)$ is shown above and the corresponding expected value is $μ_{X \\mid - 2} = \\frac{4}{3}$.\n\n> A scientific calculator is required to answer this question." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186188724 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "3cefc73e-1ad2-58be-a1de-e39c1b293d17" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186188724 #edb/ref 1073 true #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186189179 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186189203 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186189179 #edb/ref 1061 38946 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186189179 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "90a5c594-6537-5336-90c2-6eca3c31d58b" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186189179 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186189404 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186189180 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186189181 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186189180 #edb/ref 1061 38947 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186189180 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "53d73871-be25-53a5-8455-4cf04e078787" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186189180 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186188336 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186189181 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186189182 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186189181 #edb/ref 1061 38948 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186189181 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "7bbe5d6f-436a-56b7-b6c3-4b50cf86ea46" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186189181 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186188337 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186189182 #edb/ref 1061 38949 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186189182 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "e3ab0323-0d1c-5360-8b97-deeb42c28a59" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186189182 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186188338 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186189203 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186189180 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186189203 #edb/ref 1061 39321 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186189203 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "0112f403-404f-5282-8492-4ad12782a53c" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186189203 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186189410 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186189404 #edb/ref 1064 "Suppose $X$ and $Y$ are continuous random variables, where the conditional expected value of $X$ given $Y=y$ is given by $\\mu_{X \\mid y}$. In other words,\n\n$$\n\\textrm{E}\\begin{bmatrix}X\\, & \\,Y=y\\end{bmatrix} = \\mu_{X \\mid y}\n$$\n\nThe **conditional variance of $X$ given $Y=y$** is defined as\n\n$$\n\\textrm{Var}\\begin{bmatrix}X\\, & \\,Y\\end{bmatrix} = \\textrm{E}\\big\\begin{bmatrix}(X - \\mu_{X \\mid y} \\big)^2 \\, & \\, Y=y\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nAs with the discrete case, this definition can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nVar\\begin{bmatrix}X & Y = y\\end{bmatrix} &= E\\begin{bmatrix}X^{2} & Y = y\\end{bmatrix} - μ_{X \\mid y}^{2}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere\n\n$$\n\\displaystyle \\textrm{E}\\big\\begin{bmatrix}X^2 \\, & \\, Y=y \\big\\end{bmatrix} = \\int_{-\\infty}^{\\infty} x^2 \\, f_{X\\mid Y}(x \\, \\mid \\, y) \\: \\textrm{d}x\n$$\n\nand $f_{X\\mid Y}(x \\, \\mid \\, y)$ is the conditional probability density function of $X$ given $Y=y$. Note that these formulas are analogous to those for $\\textrm{Var}[X]$ for continuous $X$.\n\nWhen we select a particular value of $y$, the conditional variance of $X$ given $Y=y$ returns a real number. However, if $y$ is not specified, then\n\n$$\n\\textrm {Var}\\begin{bmatrix}X & Y = y\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\ngives us a *function* of $y$.\n\nWe have an analogous definition for the **conditional variance of $Y$ given $X=x{:}$**\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nVar\\begin{bmatrix}Y & X = x\\end{bmatrix} &= E\\begin{bmatrix}(Y - μ_{Y \\mid x})^{2} & X = x\\end{bmatrix} \\\\\n&= E\\begin{bmatrix}Y^{2} & X = x\\end{bmatrix} - μ_{Y \\mid x}^{2}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere\n\n- $\\mu_{Y \\mid x} = \\textrm{E}\\big\\begin{bmatrix}Y \\, & \\, X=x \\big\\end{bmatrix}$ is the conditional expected value of $Y$ given $X=x$,\n- $\\displaystyle \\textrm{E}\\big\\begin{bmatrix}Y^2 \\, & \\, X=x \\big\\end{bmatrix} = \\displaystyle \\int_{-\\infty}^{\\infty} y^2 \\, f_{Y\\mid X}(y \\, \\mid \\, x) \\: \\textrm{d}y$, and\n- $f_{Y\\mid X}(y \\, \\mid \\, x)$ is the conditional probability density function of $Y$ given $X=x$." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186189404 #edb/ref 1065 6444 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186189404 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "cc60678b-fd8c-537f-99be-cee66503c859" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186189404 #edb/ref 1067 "Introduction" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186189410 #edb/ref 1064 "Suppose that $X$ and $Y$ are continuous random variables. It is known that the conditional probability density function $f_{Y\\mid X}(y \\, \\mid \\, 1)$ is given by\n\n$$\n{4y^{3},\\begin{vmatrix}0 \\le y \\le 1 \\\\ 0,\\end{vmatrix}otherwise\n$$\n\nand that\n\n$$\n\\mu_{Y \\mid 1}=\\dfrac{4}{5}\n$$\n\nWhat is the conditional variance\n\n$$\n\\textrm{Var}\\big\\begin{bmatrix}Y \\, & \\, X=1\\big\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nThe conditional variance of $Y$ given $X=x$ is defined by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nVar\\begin{bmatrix}Y & X = x\\end{bmatrix} &= E\\begin{bmatrix}(Y - μ_{Y \\mid x})^{2} & X = x\\end{bmatrix} \\\\\n&= E\\begin{bmatrix}Y^{2} & X = x\\end{bmatrix} - μ_{Y \\mid x}^{2}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere\n\n$$\n\\textrm{E}\\big\\begin{bmatrix}Y^2 \\, & \\, X=x \\big\\end{bmatrix} = \\int_{-\\infty}^{\\infty} y^2 \\, f_{Y\\mid X}(y \\, \\mid \\, x) \\: \\textrm{d}y\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nE\\begin{bmatrix}Y^{2} & X = 1\\end{bmatrix} &= \\int_{- ∞}^{∞}y^{2}f_{Y\\mid X}(y \\mid 1)dy \\\\\n&= \\int_{0}^{1}y^{2} \\cdot 4y^{3}dx \\\\\n&= \\int_{0}^{1}4y^{5}dy \\\\\n&= [\\frac{2y^{6}}{3}]_{0}^{1} \\\\\n&= \\frac{2}{3}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nVar\\begin{bmatrix}Y & X = 1\\end{bmatrix} &= E\\begin{bmatrix}Y^{2} & X = 1\\end{bmatrix} - μ_{Y \\mid 1}^{2} \\\\\n&= \\frac{2}{3} - (\\frac{4}{5})^{2} \\\\\n&= \\frac{2}{3} - \\frac{16}{25} \\\\\n&= \\frac{2}{75}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186189410 #edb/ref 1065 6490 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186189410 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "51fd1dbf-d36f-5e8c-b62b-ede292dae6da" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186189410 #edb/ref 1067 "A Worked Example" #edb/ref 17592186045417]}
